1. First, we will sort the data by the source airline carrier (column 'den', 'aa', 'co', etc.) and the timestamp (act_dep_time). This will help us group the flights by their respective airlines.

```bash
sort -t $'\t' -k2,2 -k3,3n data.txt > sorted_data.txt
```

  2. Next, we will use awk to extract the airline and act_dep_time columns from the sorted file and store them in separate arrays for each airline. This will allow us to count on-time arrivals more efficiently.

```bash
awk -F'\t' '{if ($2 == "den") {arr["den"][$3]=$4}} END {for (airline in arr) print airline, length(arr[airline])}' sorted_data.txt
```

  3. Finally, we will loop through the arrays and count the number of on-time arrivals for each airline. In this example, an on-time arrival is defined as a flight that arrived within 15 minutes of its scheduled departure time.

```bash
for airline in arr; do
    on_time=0
    for dep_time in arr[$airline]; do
        if [ $(date -d "$dep_time" +%s) -le $(date -d "1900-03-31 11:45:00Z" +%s) ] && [ $(date -d "$dep_time" +%s) -ge $(date -d "1900-03-31 10:55:00Z" +%s) ]; then
            on_time=$((on_time+1))
        fi
    done
    echo "$airline has $on_time on-time arrivals."
done
```

  4. Combine the above commands into a single bash script:

```bash
#!/bin/bash

sort -t $'\t' -k2,2 -k3,3n data.txt > sorted_data.txt
awk -F'\t' '{if ($2 == "den") {arr["den"][$3]=$4}} END {for (airline in arr) print airline, length(arr[airline])}' sorted_data.txt > airlines.txt

on_time=0
for airline in $(cat airlines.txt | awk '{print $1}' | sort -u); do
    on_time=0
    for dep_time in $(cat airlines.txt | grep "$airline" | cut -f4); do
        if [ $(date -d "$dep_time" +%s) -le $(date -d "1900-03-31 11:45:00Z" +%s) ] && [ $(date -d "$dep_time" +%s) -ge $(date -d "1900-03-31 10:55:00Z" +%s) ]; then
            on_time=$((on_time+1))
        fi
    done
    echo "$airline has $on_time on-time arrivals."
done
```

This script will generate the desired output, grouping flights by source airline carrier and counting the number of on-time arrivals.
